title: Wybory do Sejmu
new-page: true
call: polish_opening_state
on-arrival: {!
// The monthly router enters here after processing the month, before another
// ordinary action. Re-entry resumes the saved phase instead of creating a vote.
if (Q.polish_election_system && Q.sejm_election_due &&
        (!Q.sejm_pending || Q.sejm_pending.phase === 'complete')) {
    Q.sejm_pending = {
        id: 'sejm_' + Q.year + '_' + Q.month + '_' + (Q.n_elections + 1),
        year: Q.year, month: Q.month,
        first: !Q.sejm_first_election_completed, phase: 'pending'
    };
    Q.in_election = 1;
}
!}
go-to: results if sejm_forming_government; main if not sejm_election_in_progress

= Wybory do Sejmu — [+ month : month +] [+ year +]

[? if not sejm_first_election_completed : The Sejm election of 5 November 1922 is now due. Voting, results and government formation are compressed into one November sequence. The result also constitutes a simplified 111-seat Senate in the same party proportions; it is recorded once, not a separate campaign. ChZJN contests as a joint ZLN–PSChD list. ?]

[? if not sejm_first_election_completed : Campaigning and monthly effects determine voting intentions. We will record those votes once, allocate **444 MPs**, and then consider governments. A majority requires **223 MPs**. Reading these screens and choosing a government does not spend another monthly action. ?]

[? if sejm_first_election_completed : The five-year term of the Sejm elected in 1922 has ended. Under the game's default legal calendar the election was ordered the next day and is held on Sunday 19 February 1928, the first Sunday at least 78 days later. This is a gameplay calendar, not the historical election date. The same 444-seat method applies, every list stands on its own and no German thresholds or bans apply. ?]

[? if sejm_first_election_completed : This is the next lawful Sejm election after 1922. Its certified result ends the first chapter: no new government is formed in this chapter, and a report follows. ?]

- @calculate: Count the votes.

@calculate
go-to: election_algorithm
set-jump: sejm_election.allocate

@allocate
call: sejm_election_result
go-to: results if sejm_election_error = ""; error if sejm_election_error != ""

@error
new-page: true

= The election could not be calculated

[+ sejm_election_error +]

No parliamentary seats, election counter or history were changed. This indicates invalid simulation data, not an election outcome.

- @calculate: Retry the calculation.

@results
new-page: true
call: polish_opening_state
go-to: main if not sejm_has_result; government if sejm_has_result and not pl_chapter_ended; chapter_end if sejm_has_result and pl_chapter_ended
on-display: {!
// Z — 0.73: the hemicycle and the table of the results card, from the same list rows as the Library's chart.
if (typeof d3 !== 'undefined' && typeof window !== 'undefined' && document.getElementById('sejm_result_chart')) {
    var width = 500;
    var height = 500;
    var screenWidth = document.getElementById('content').offsetWidth;
    if (screenWidth < width - 50) {
        width = screenWidth - 50;
        height = width;
        document.getElementById('sejm_result_chart').style.height = screenWidth / 2 + 'px';
    }
    var parliament = d3.parliament();
    parliament.width(width).height(height).innerRadiusCoef(0.4);
    parliament.enter.fromCenter(true).smallToBig(true);
    parliament.exit.toCenter(false).bigToSmall(true);
    d3.select('#sejm_result_chart').datum(Q.sejm_display_rows.map(function(row) {
        return {id: row.id, legend: row.name, name: row.name, seats: row.seats};
    })).call(parliament);
    var table = d3.select('#sejm_result_table').append('table').attr('class', 'pl-result');
    table.append('thead').append('tr').selectAll('th')
        .data(['', 'List', 'Votes %', 'MPs', 'Change']).enter().append('th').text(function(value) { return value; });
    var body = table.append('tbody');
    for (var row of Q.sejm_display_rows) {
        d3.select('#sejm_result_chart').selectAll('.seat.' + row.id).style('fill', Q.sejm_chart_colors[row.id]);
        var change = Q.sejm_seat_changes ? Q.sejm_seat_changes[row.id] : null;
        var tr = body.append('tr').classed('pl-pps', row.id === 'pps');
        tr.append('td').append('span').attr('class', 'box').style('background-color', Q.sejm_chart_colors[row.id]);
        tr.append('td').text(row.name);
        tr.append('td').text(row.votes.toFixed(1));
        tr.append('td').text(row.seats);
        tr.append('td').text(change === null || change === undefined ? '—' : change > 0 ? '+' + change : change < 0 ? '\u2212' + (-change) : '0');
    }
    var total = table.append('tfoot').append('tr');
    total.append('td');
    total.append('td').text('Total');
    total.append('td');
    total.append('td').text(Q.sejm_total_seats);
    total.append('td');
}
!}

= Sejm election result — [+ sejm_result_date +]

The most votes went to [+ sejm_largest_lists +].

{!<svg id="sejm_result_chart" style="width: 100%; max-width: 500px; height: 250px;"> </svg>!}

{!<div id="sejm_result_table"></div>!}

[? if pl_joint_lists_display : Joint lists at this election: [+ pl_joint_lists_display +]. A joint list shares its MPs among its parties in proportion to their votes; each party keeps its own club, its relations and its own place in a cabinet. ?]

[? if sejm_has_chzjn and not pl_joint_lists_display : ChZJN is shown together, but ZLN and PSChD remain separate parties for relations and cabinet membership; its MPs are shared in proportion to their votes. ?]

@government
call: polish_opening_state

= Government formation

The new Sejm has [+ sejm_total_seats +] MPs; a majority needs [+ sejm_majority_required +]. PPS has [+ pps_seats +] MPs. The previous cabinet governs as caretaker until the head of state appoints a new one.

PPS now makes one offer: a cabinet and its prime minister, the role of PPS, a request for minority support and the PPS portfolios. Each partner answers yes or no with its reason. A cabinet without PPS is formed if PPS stays in opposition or its offer fails. ChZJN was an electoral list, not an obligation to govern together. In December the Sejm elects its Marshal and the National Assembly elects the President, without changing the cabinet.

- @polish_cabinet_formation: Continue to the government formation.
- @return_to_play: Continue.

@return_to_play
view-if: not sejm_forming_government
go-to: root

@chapter_end
on-arrival: {!
// The election sequence is complete; the chapter report replaces any government formation (19.1).
if (Q.sejm_pending && Q.sejm_pending.phase === 'results' && Q.S.chapter.status === 'ended') {
    Q.sejm_pending.phase = 'complete';
    Q.in_election = 0;
}
!}

= The chapter ends

The result above is certified: 444 MPs and the simplified Senate are recorded. This was the next lawful Sejm election after 1922, so the first chapter ends here, before a new government is formed.

- @polish_chapter_report: Read the chapter report.

@finish
call: polish_opening_state
on-arrival: {!
if (Q.sejm_pending && Q.sejm_pending.phase === 'results' && Q.sejm_pending.government_choice) {
    Q.sejm_pending.phase = 'complete';
    Q.in_election = 0;
}
!}

PPS position: [+ pps_government_position +].

This completes the election sequence without spending a monthly action. Parliamentary results remain fixed between elections. The Marshal and the President are elected in December; the cabinet stays in office. Inherited Prussian executive powers remain unavailable. The Polish economy, budget and state cards follow the portfolios of the new cabinet.

- @root: Resume play.
